    id: "lore_founding_charter",
    title: "MEGACITY FOUNDING CHARTER — FRAGMENT",
    category: "city-history",
    itemType: "classified-file",
    rarity: "rare",
    author: "Emergency Governance Council",
    content: "ARTICLE 1: In recognition of the catastrophic failure of all prior governmental institutions, the Emergency Governance Council hereby establishes the Megacity Administrative Authority. All previous laws, regulations, and constitutional provisions are suspended indefinitely. ARTICLE 2: Executive authority shall be vested in a City Commander, appointed by the Council, serving at the Council's pleasure. The Commander shall possess absolute administrative discretion in matters of: public safety, resource allocation, population management, and 'such other matters as circumstance requires.' ARTICLE 3: Civil liberties shall be restored 'at the earliest practicable date.' [Note: This article has been amended forty-seven times. Each amendment extends the definition of 'practicable.' The current estimated restoration date is classified.]",
    flavorText: "The ink is faded but the implications are still sharp.",
