    id: "lore_last_war_journal",
    title: "PRIVATE JOURNAL — SGT. ELENA VOSS",
    category: "pre-war",
    itemType: "journal",
    rarity: "uncommon",
    author: "Sgt. Elena Voss, 14th Urban Defense Battalion",
    content: "Day 1: Orders received. We're pulling back to the megacity perimeter. Everything outside the wall is being abandoned. Three million people live out there. Command says 'acceptable losses.' I don't know what's acceptable about it.\n\nDay 4: The shelling started at dawn. The eastern suburbs are gone. Just... gone. Smoke column visible from sixty kilometers.\n\nDay 7: Refugees at the gates. Thousands. Command says let them in. Then Command says stop letting them in. Then Command goes silent. We opened the gates anyway. Court martial be damned.\n\nDay 12: Sector Zero detonated. The flash was visible through the walls. Geiger counters screaming. This is how the world ends — not with silence, but with paperwork and mushroom clouds.\n\nDay 15: No more entries after this. We're being reassigned to 'population management.' I don't want to know what that means.",
    flavorText: "The last few pages are blank. The pen was left clipped to the spine.",
    zoneTypes: ["ruins", "military", "wasteland"]
