    id: "lore_reactor7_report",
    title: "INCIDENT REPORT: REACTOR CORE 7 ANOMALY",
    category: "science",
    itemType: "classified-file",
    rarity: "rare",
    author: "Chief Engineer Dr. Malik Torres (DECEASED)",
    content: "CLASSIFICATION: ULTRA — EYES ONLY\n\nAt 0347 hours, Reactor Core 7 experienced a Category 5 thermal excursion. All automated safety systems failed simultaneously. Manual shutdown was initiated but overridden by... the reactor itself. There is no other way to describe it. The control rods withdrew against hydraulic pressure. The coolant flow reversed direction. Core temperature reached 4,200°C — well beyond design limits — and then STABILIZED.\n\nThe reactor is operating at 340% rated output with zero structural degradation. This is physically impossible.\n\nRecommendation: Immediate shutdown and investigation.\n\nAddendum (handwritten): Recommendation denied by administration. 'The city needs the power.' God help us all.\n\nAddendum 2 (different handwriting): Dr. Torres found dead in his quarters. Natural causes. Investigation closed.",
    flavorText: "Someone circled 'Natural causes' and wrote 'LIES' in red ink.",
    zoneTypes: ["industrial", "anomaly"]
