    title: "THE AUTHORITY — ENFORCEMENT HANDBOOK (3rd Ed.)",
    category: "faction-intel",
    itemType: "book",
    rarity: "common",
    author: "Authority Training Division",
    content: "CHAPTER 7: SUSPECT INTERACTION PROTOCOLS\n\nSection 7.1: All citizens are to be addressed as 'citizen' unless their crime warrants the designation 'perp,' 'suspect,' or 'convict.' Informal address is prohibited.\n\nSection 7.3: The use of reasonable force is authorized at the officer's discretion. 'Reasonable' is defined as 'sufficient to achieve compliance.' There is no upper limit specified.\n\nSection 7.5: Miranda rights are to be read in full. Officers may read at any speed. Current departmental record: 4.2 seconds.\n\nSection 7.8: Suspects who request legal representation will be provided with a public defender within 30 days. Trials are scheduled within 48 hours. The scheduling discrepancy is a known issue.\n\nAPPENDIX C: Approved Interrogation Techniques\n[Pages 47 through 93 have been removed from this copy. Stamp reads: 'FOR SENIOR OFFICERS ONLY']",
    flavorText: "Dog-eared at Chapter 7. Someone underlined 'no upper limit' twice.",
    zoneTypes: ["ruins", "military", "industrial"]
