    id: "lore_gene_wright_thesis",
    title: "DR. HELIX — DOCTORAL THESIS (REJECTED)",
    category: "science",
    itemType: "data-disk",
    rarity: "rare",
    author: "Dr. Lyssa Helix (pre-defection)",
    content: "TITLE: 'Directed Somatic Mutation as a Response to Environmental Toxicity: A Framework for Adaptive Human Evolution'\n\nABSTRACT:\n'The post-collapse environment presents mutagenic pressures that conventional medicine cannot address. Rather than treating radiation damage, toxic exposure, and pathogenic adaptation as diseases, this paper proposes reframing them as evolutionary opportunities.\n\nThe human genome contains approximately 20,000 protein-coding genes. Of these, fewer than 2,000 are actively expressed in any given cell. The remaining 18,000 are potential — dormant capabilities waiting for the right environmental pressure, or the right scientist, to activate them.'\n\nREJECTION NOTICE:\n'This thesis is rejected on ethical grounds. The proposed framework would require human experimentation on a scale that violates every medical protocol in existence. The review board is unanimous.'\n\nHandwritten note in margin: 'Ethics are a luxury of the pre-war world. Survival is the only ethic that matters now. — L.H.'",
