    id: "lore_sector_zero",
    title: "SURVEY REPORT — SECTOR ZERO PERIMETER",
    category: "wasteland",
    itemType: "classified-file",
    rarity: "rare",
    author: "Reconnaissance Unit 7 (all members now deceased)",
    content: "SURVEY MISSION: Sector Zero Perimeter Assessment\nCLASSIFICATION: RESTRICTED\n\nFindings: The detonation crater extends 4.7km in diameter. Radiation levels at the perimeter exceed 850 mSv/hr — lethal exposure within 15 minutes without full hazmat. The Glass Desert begins at the crater's edge: silica fused into obsidian-like sheets by the thermal pulse. Extends 12km in every direction.\n\nAnomalies noted:\n- Structures within the blast radius that should have been vaporized remain standing. Their materials have been... altered. They appear to be the same buildings but composed of unknown crystalline structures.\n- Geiger readings fluctuate in regular patterns. 3-second intervals. Like a heartbeat.\n- At the crater's exact center, satellite imaging shows a structure that was NOT present before the detonation. It is approximately 200m tall. It is growing.\n\nRecommendation: Establish permanent exclusion zone. Increase perimeter to 25km. Do not send further survey teams.\n\nNote appended by Central Command: 'Recommendation partially adopted. Survey team reassigned. Medical records sealed.'",
    flavorText: "The paper crackles with residual static. Don't hold it for too long.",
