    id: "lore_pre_war_school",
    title: "TEXTBOOK — 'OUR BEAUTIFUL CITY' (CHILDREN'S EDITION)",
    category: "pre-war",
    itemType: "book",
    rarity: "common",
    author: "Department of Education (Pre-War)",
    content: "CHAPTER 1: WELCOME TO OUR CITY!\n\n'Our city is the greatest place in the world! With its tall buildings, clean streets, and friendly neighbors, it's a wonderful place to grow up.\n\nDid you know? Our city has:\n- 47 parks and recreation areas!\n- 200 schools with the best teachers!\n- Free healthcare for all citizens!\n- Clean drinking water from our award-winning treatment plants!\n\nCOLOR THE PICTURE: Can you color the happy family in their spacious apartment? Don't forget the pet dog!\n\nFUN FACT: Our city's government works hard every day to make sure everyone is safe and happy. The Mayor says: 'Every child is our future!' What a great place to live!'\n\n[The remaining pages are water-damaged beyond readability. Someone has written on the inside back cover: 'They lied about everything. — M.S., Year One']",
